{"title":"2006 iTest Problems/Problem U4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>The following problem is from the Ultimate Question of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a>, where solving this problem required the answer of a previous problem. When the problem is rewritten, the T-value is substituted.</i>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> ranges over the integers, the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b455cb969c8649ed1f35ce89cd0ae90fb45995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^4 - 898n^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" /> evaluates to just one prime number. Find this prime.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30f88b6db5dad993913cb2ee3b1b9dcb14bc620e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$898$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is two away from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd4beaeec1aa15c400a0763d78937b0385924b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$900$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. We can add and subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd6917e1a598e7efad0531d69a9cf51badfe01d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n^2$\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" /> in the original expression to help factorization while maintaining equality.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/3/0c3f841b5cd151182719037d38cfea2af9b2c2f0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} n^4 - 898n^2 + 1 &amp;= n^4 + 2n^2 + 1 - 2n^2 - 898n^2 \\\\ &amp;= n^4 + 2n^2 + 1 - 900n^2 \\\\ &amp;= (n^2 + 1)^2 - (30n)^2 \\\\ &amp;= (n^2 + 30n + 1)(n^2 - 30n + 1) \\end{align*}\" width=\"370\" height=\"102\" />\nIf none of the two factors are equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b455cb969c8649ed1f35ce89cd0ae90fb45995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^4 - 898n^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" /> is a composite number. If either one of the factors is set to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> would not be an integer. If either one of the factors is set to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/1/6610a8c2e01c86d4c5dd19c242f6070c0a7633e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = -30,0,30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6fc266463b33c8b1c079a50909f3fd03ed5ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, while plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/0/1106a8c399bc50cabdfa241f4c6999759bc80560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 30$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abaa69694b819d99b11085ab959fbd83c9bbccc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = -30$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524276ab192005c9192135c35648c864acafa1d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1801$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. From the description (or doing a prime check), the wanted prime number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/2/f4212c0e4e46cc8756c7b0292176cb83ab1acbe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{1801}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Sieve of Nygard will easily show that 1801 is prime. \n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U3\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem U3\">Problem U3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_U5\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem U5\">Problem U5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colsp